Your report said ipc_proofs: 10 passed. I independently re-ran it 6 times, and it fails deterministically:

  test running_turn_socket_tool_receives_published_outcome ... FAILED (ipc_proofs.rs:224), "9 passed; 1 failed".

Root cause: the test never calls begin_turn, so active_turn is None and `publish("", id, ..)` falls into the `None => slots.insert(("", id), Ready)` branch; wait_for(("turn-live", id)) never sees it and times out. That branch is also the original H1 leak (an unclearable ("", id) Ready slot).

Fix in one pass, amend, rerun:
1. Make the test mirror production: call `executor.begin_turn(&turn.turn_id)` (production does this in start_driving). Verify every production path that starts driving a turn (including scheduler promote_next / queued turns) goes through begin_turn; report the call sites.
2. Remove the leak: an empty-turn-id publish must never create a ("", id) slot. If no active turn exists, drop it (with a tracing warn). Add a test: publish("", id) with no active turn leaves slot_count()==0.
3. Paste the RAW `test result:` lines of every test target in the final report (copy them from the command output, do not summarize). Run the full gate command once more right before reporting.
